  "word_count": 109,
  "text_content": "Amaka lives on a small farm with her Papa. They have a white goat that loves to eat grass. Every morning, Amaka brings fresh water for the goat. One afternoon, the gate was open. The goat walked out of the farm and went down the road. Amaka looked for her in the yard. She looked around the house. The goat was not there. Amaka began to cry. Then she heard a soft sound from the road. She ran to the gate and looked outside. The goat was standing in the grass, chewing slowly. Amaka hugged her goat and led her back home. Now Papa shuts the gate every night.",
